          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'The aim of the game is to avoid capturing any Jacks in tricks, especially the Jack of Spades (Polignac). Penalty points are scored for each Jack taken; the first player to reach the agreed total loses the game.',
          gameplay: 'Eldest hand leads first. Players must follow suit if possible; otherwise may play any card. The highest card of the suit led wins the trick. The winner of each trick leads to the next. There are no trumps. Players incur penalty points for capturing Jacks.',
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit when possible; otherwise any card may be played.',
            'Highest card of the suit led wins the trick; winner leads next.',
            'No trumps.',
            'Jack of Spades (Polignac) costs 2 penalty points; each other Jack costs 1.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Dump your Jacks! If you can't follow suit, play your Jacks immediately to ensure an opponent captures them. Save your lowest cards (7s and 8s) for the end of the round, as this is when the 'Big Jacks' usually come out as players run out of suit-fillers.",
          intermediate: "The 'Polignac Trap': If you hold the Queen, King, or Ace of Spades, you are in danger of winning the Polignac. Try to lead Spades early in the round while everyone still has low Spades (7, 8, 9). This 'Clears' the suit and forces the person with the Jack to play it early when you aren't forced to win it.",
          advanced: "The 'Capot' (Slam): In some house rules, if you capture ALL FOUR Jacks, you score zero points and everyone else gets 5. If you have a massive hand of high cards, you might intentionally 'Vacuum' up the Jacks to trigger this bonus. However, if you miss even one, you will have a disastrous score. It's the 'Shoot the Moon' of Polignac.",
          tips: [
            "Don't lead a suit you are 'Short' in (only 1 or 2 cards), as you want to keep that suit so you can 'Follow' safely later.",
            "Watch the 'Polignac' card. Once it is played, the game becomes much safer for the high-card holders.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
